@251 = ~Flame Strike (Evocation)
Level: 5
Sphere: combat
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: target creature
Saving Throw: half

When the priest calls down a flame strike spell, a vertical column of fire roars downward striking the exact location called for by the caster. The target must roll a save vs. spell. Failure means the creature sustains 1d8 points of damage per level of the caster (maximum 20D8); otherwise, the damage is halved.~
@252 = ~Flame Strike (Evocation)
Level: 5
Sphere: combat
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: target creature
Saving Throw: half

When the priest calls down a flame strike spell, a vertical column of fire roars downward striking the exact location called for by the caster. The target must roll a save vs. spell. Failure means the creature sustains 24d8 points of damage (26d8 at level 30 and 28d8 at level 40); otherwise, the damage is halved.~
@2521 = ~Hellish Flame Strike~
@2522 = ~Hellish Flame Strike (Conjuration)
Level: 5
Sphere: combat, evil
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: 5-meter radius
Saving Throw: half

Fire from the infernal planes strikes the target, dealing 20D6 +20 points of damage. Nearby creatures also suffer damage from the sulfurous vapors released by the impact. A successful save vs. spell at a -2 penalty (an additional -1 for every 5 levels of the caster beyond level 20) halves the damage.~

@254 = ~Animal Summoning II (Conjuration/Summoning)
Level: 5
Sphere: animal, summoning
Range: 30 meters
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: special
Saving Throw: none

The caster can summon up to 3 creatures with 8 Hit Dice or less. Fire creatures and creatures with an affinity for fire answer the Fire Lord's call in place of the animals normally summoned.
The summoned creatures aid the caster by any means available. They stay until the battle ends, their task is complete, the caster is safe, they are dismissed, or the spell expires.~
