@259 = ~Fire Mark~
@2510 = ~Fire Mark (Alteration)
Level: 5
Sphere: charm, elemental (fire)
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell removes a creature's fire resistance or immunity. A creature with no fire resistance instead becomes vulnerable and takes double fire damage.
Two Fire Marks can stack, making even a normally immune creature vulnerable. The spell is treated as a curse and checks the target's magic resistance as though it were 30% lower.~
@25101 = ~Fire Mark (Alteration)
Level: 5
Sphere: charm, elemental (fire)
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 25 rounds
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell removes a creature's fire resistance or immunity. A creature with no fire resistance instead becomes vulnerable and takes double fire damage.
Two Fire Marks can stack, making even a normally immune creature vulnerable. The spell is treated as a curse and bypasses the target's magic resistance.~
@25102 = ~Reduced Fire Resistance~

@2511 = ~Explosive Combustion~
@2512 = ~Explosive Combustion (Evocation, Necromancy)
Level: 5
Sphere: necromancy, elemental, fire
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: radius 9 meters
Saving Throw: special

This spell suddenly sets all creatures in the area ablaze. The brief but intense combustion destroys weaker creatures outright. Stronger creatures suffer the following effects:

1 or 2 HD: Explosion
3 or 4 HD: Explosion, death if saving throw is successful
5 or 6 HD: Death, 8D6 points of damage if saving throw is successful
7 or 8 HD: 8D6 points of damage, 4D6 if saving throw is successful
9 HD or more: 4D6 points of damage, no damage on a successful save.

The creatures that explode are reduced to dust and leave no corpse. They cause an explosion of 8 meters radius that inflicts 4D6 points of fire damage (saving throw to halve) to all creatures within the area.
The creatures who "die" are turned into ashes by a smaller explosion, which extends over 5 meters and inflicts 2D6 points of fire damage (saving throw to halve).
Creatures that survive the explosion suffer fire damage, as indicated in the above table.
Saves against the initial effect are made at -2, with an additional -1 for every 5 caster levels beyond level 20. Saves to halve damage from the resulting explosions receive no penalty.
Undead, cold creatures and fire creatures are immune to this spell.~

@2513 = ~Pulverization~
@2514 = ~Pulverization (Alteration)
Level: 5
Sphere: elemental (fire)
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: hemisphere 6.5-meter radius
Saving Throw: half

When the preacher of flames casts this spell, the soil at the targeted area heats up to its breaking point before exploding, throwing fire and burning embers on all nearby creatures. Each suffers an impact per caster level, each one inflicting 1D4 points of crushing damage and 1D2 points of fire damage (maximum 15D4 + 15D2). A save vs. spell avoids half of the impacts.
Only stone explodes; wood and flesh burn without exploding. Since the spell targets the ground rather than living creatures, magic resistance offers no protection.~
@25141 = ~Pulverization (Alteration)
Level: 5
Sphere: elemental (fire)
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: hemisphere 6.5-meter radius
Saving Throw: half

When the preacher of flames casts this spell, the soil at the targeted area heats up to its breaking point before exploding, throwing fire and burning embers on all nearby creatures. They suffer 15D4 points of crushing damage and 18D2 points of fire damage (20D2 points at level 30, 21D2 at level 40). A save vs. breath weapon avoids half of the impacts.
The spell leaves a small crater. Only stone explodes; wood and flesh burn without exploding. Since the spell targets the ground rather than living creatures, magic resistance offers no protection.~
