When the preacher of flames casts this spell, the soil at the targeted area heats up to its breaking point before exploding, throwing fire and burning embers on all nearby creatures. They suffer 15D4 points of crushing damage and 15D2 points of fire damage. A save vs. breath weapon at -2 (an additional -1 for every 5 levels of the caster beyond level 20) avoids half of the impacts.
The spell leaves a small crater. Only stone explodes; wood and flesh burn without exploding. Since the spell targets the ground rather than living creatures, magic resistance offers no protection.~

@2515 = ~Mass Protection From Fire~
@2516 = ~Mass Protection From Fire (Abjuration)
Level: 5
Sphere: protection, elemental
Range: 30 meters
Duration: 3 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 9-meter radius
Saving Throw: none

This spell grants the preacher's party complete immunity to normal fire (torches, bonfires, burning oil, and the like) and 80% resistance to magical fire (dragon breath, fire spells, and similar effects). It may be cast on an area; only party members inside are protected. Enemies are unaffected.~

